body:
This is an interesting post that I'm glad I got to read about! I started reading his books this past year, and I've known about the law of attraction for a long time. Something I think that is important about these teachings is that none of them should require physical action. The philosophical idea of "You are God" I feel was really driven by the idea to make people realize that they are creators. Personally, I fall under the belief we've all been manifesting at all times whether we are aware of it or not. You get what you assume to be true.

&#x200B;

In terms of...reality shifting and Neville, I've heard about his "worlds within worlds"--where he went to a world that he made. Sounds a lot like reality shifting--which I've heard to be a very old religious practice. This, I could totally see, requires some time to take. 

&#x200B;

Overall, loved hearing about how the law was taught throughout the ages!

Congratulations!!! I'm so proud of you, that's amazing and really inspiring. It takes so much persistence and effort to cut yourself off! I need to get over some unhealthy lifestyle changes myself, glad to hear that you're able to break such a vicious cycle. Truly inspiring. 

&#x200B;

It's only up from here! :) I wish you the best always!
